\section*{Hahn–Wilson thick generation at fp-type two}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For sufficiently large primes, a connective p-complete spectrum of exact fp-type two is claimed not finitely constructible from standard BP<2>, despite satisfying both finite-localization and telescope-to-Morava comparison equivalences. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 319, 2026-09-26): Large-prime algebraicity transfers the problem to periodic sheaf complexes, where Laurent operators create paired defects growing faster than the available kernel bounds. The resulting homology-to-dual-homology restriction removes each possible finite tower stage by backward induction, including retracts. Completion remains locally controlled, allowing a connective cover with the required fp-type and localization equivalences while preserving the global obstruction.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 319, 2026-09-26): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed counterexample to that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
